// @run
// @log true
// A LITERAL-UNION type argument in a generic alias instance (`Holder<K>` where
// `type K = "a" | "b"`). The instance's field is code 0 — an interned i32 ATOM, not
// an i32/boolean — and `sFieldIsLitUnion` keys that off the field's recorded union
// NAME. The generic-instance interner (`gaeEnsure`) carried its own hand-copied
// element-name dispatch with only four arms (15 / 5 / 16 / 4), so a code-0 field
// recorded "" — the row read back as a PLAIN i32 slot and the member literal `"a"`
// emitted as a string ref into it. INVALID WASM on master ("failed to parse
// WebAssembly module"), the exact shared-layout/different-encoding split
// `annShapeIndexOf`'s own code-0 comment describes for the inline-shape path.
//
// D-ELEMHOME gives the element-name table ONE home: `gaeEnsure` delegates every
// code but 5 to `shapeFieldElemName`, so the generic instance records the union name
// the inline-shape and declared-struct interners already recorded.
type K = "a" | "b"
type Holder<T> = { k: T }

const h: Holder<K> = { k: "a" }
print(h.k == "a")
